Divergence anchor

The point where this fork departed from upstream is marked by an
annotated tag whose name embeds the actual fork date, in the form
fork-point-YYYY-MM-DD. Always look the tag up instead of trusting any
date written down elsewhere:

    git tag -l 'fork-point-*'

(Example current value: fork-point-2026-10-15. The tag is the source of
truth; the example only illustrates the naming scheme.)

